                <pb facs="0663" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/517: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-21T15:00:00+08:00">February 21, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 21—10:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. My 102, February 14, 11 a.m. I understand British Embassy, complying with
                    instructions from London, will tell Kung this evening that British Government
                    strongly disapproves the proposed instructions to Maze because they confront
                    Commissioners with alternatives of signing [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >resigrdng?</hi>] or breaking the formal integrity of the customs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
